// A host that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error for connect
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Strings the host reads): getaddrinfo() reads the name
// only up to the NUL, so the call would connect to a different host. The port
// is never reached.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: host-string connect
print "before";
connect("127.0.0.1" + chr(0) + "tail", 1);
